{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ACCEPTANCE EVIDENCE — HARNESS FULLY GREEN ON A NATIVE AMD64 RUNNER.\nRun: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/30512622682, job 'jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)', ARCHITECTURE: ubuntu-latest = native x86_64 (naming the arch per this story's own AC), on merged commit b4014703a.\nEVERY STEP SUCCEEDED:\n  Build and start the Jira DC harness .......... SUCCESS  (built from the VENDORED Dockerfile; 'Container live_jira_dc-jira-dc-1 Started', 'Volume live_jira_dc_jira-dc-m2-cache Creating')\n  Wait for Jira DC to become ready ............. SUCCESS  ('Jira DC ready after 37 tries' -> ~3 minutes at 5s cadence, comfortably inside the 20-minute budget)\n  Run the Jira DC harness smoke tests .......... SUCCESS  ('4 passed in 5.65s')\n  Jira DC container logs on failure ............ skipped  (nothing failed)\n  Tear down the Jira DC harness ................ SUCCESS  (docker compose down -v)\nTotal job wall-clock ~7 minutes.\n\nAC-BY-AC:\n * AC1 harness BUILDS (not pulls) and starts, readiness probe reports REST answering -> YES, both steps green; readiness satisfied in 37 polls.\n * AC2 smoke test creates and reads back an issue via REST v2, and a PAT-authenticated request succeeds -> YES, all 4 tests pass. That set includes the REST v2 create/read round trip asserting the ROUND-TRIPPED VALUES (and that description comes back a plain STRING, proving v2/wiki not v3/ADF), PAT bearer auth with a token minted programmatically via POST /rest/pat/latest/tokens, the bogus-token contrast case, and the serverInfo assertion that it is a Jira 8.x deployment with deploymentType != Cloud.\n * AC3 teardown: every created issue 404s from its DIRECT endpoint, search never consulted -> YES; teardown green, and the poll-to-404 runs unconditionally on every branch.\n * AC4 default suite collects zero from the harness; Makefile test: target unmodified -> verified locally (collect-only: 4 deselected, 0 collected) and by git diff.\n * Structural ACs (digest pin, both mandatory entrypoint flags, no dud flags, loopback bind, platform, tty/stdin_open, m2 cache, no integration marker) -> 13 unit-tier tests, mutation-verified, running on EVERY commit.\n * README records the pinned digest, the runtime Maven dependency, the 8.x-only constraint, the amd64 requirement, the opt-in invocation, and the drift limitation naming 9895-ac7d-4276-4f08.\n\nTHREE LIVE RUNS, each failure mine and each fixed:\n  run 1 (30507727332): built + booted + ready; 3/4 tests; hardcoded project template rejected 400.\n  run 2 (30508956696): 4/4 tests; teardown failed on a cascaded delete (404).\n  run 3 (30512622682): 4/4 tests AND clean teardown. GREEN.\nThe harness design was never the problem — the amd64 diagnosis and the build-not-pull correction both held on first contact with a real runner."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785384387391497001,"uuid":"59fae304-f23c-43c3-abb1-1e03afcdaf4d"}